-- title:
--   Row-10 inverse cubic and Newton approximant polynomials
-- statement:
--   These are explicit finite coefficient data for the degree-10 inverse cubic of a fifth power of $z^3-z-\beta$. The algebraic parameter used in the later proofs satisfies $\alpha^3=1001/20-66\alpha+21\alpha^2$. The bundle defines the inverse cubic $G(t,v)$ and degree-at-most-31 polynomials $P_\alpha(t)$ and $Q_\alpha(t)$, with coefficients of the form $a+b\alpha+c\alpha^2$ for rational $a,b,c$. The variables are $t=z^{-2}$ and $v=\beta/z^3$.
--
--   The later analytic construction uses
--   $$v=P_\alpha(t)+t^{32}Y(t).$$
--   The residual identity and inverse-derivative identity for these finite polynomials are proved in separate theorem records; they are not assumptions attached to the definitions.
-- source:
--   https://gist.github.com/Amal-David/adce933460b7501cb123f483f62775eb/f5a76eda649f3e995a8ec6b98387b23b64c6debb#file-fifth-md; H5_COMPLETE_CHAIN.md, Sections 1–4; lower/H5_LOWER_MIDDLE_COMPLETION.md and upper/H5_UPPER_BRIDGE.md in the archived research checkpoint. The finite Newton coefficient arrays are auxiliary exact certificates constructed for the accompanying Lean formalization, and are specified in full by this definition submission.

